_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.012828669992112962,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":45.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0888419859236953,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":69.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06538366920439531,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":83.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.04975193713316406,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007473312527550245,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.00527,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Primerica, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides financial products and services to middle-income households in the United States and Canada. It operates in three segments: Term Life Insurance; Investment and Savings Products; and Corporate and Other Distributed Products. The Term Life Insurance segment underwrites individual term life insurance products. The Investment and Savings Products segment provides mutual funds and various retirement plans, managed investments, variable and fixed annuities, and fixed indexed annuities; and offers segregated funds. The Corporate and Other Distributed Products segment provides mortgage loans; prepaid legal services that assist subscribers with legal matters, such as drafting wills, living wills and powers of attorney, trial defense, and motor vehicle-related matters; ID theft defense services; auto and homeowners' insurance; home automation solutions; and insurance products, including supplemental and accidental death, and disability insurance. It distributes and sells its products through licensed sales representatives to middle-income households. Primerica, Inc. was founded in 1927 and is headquartered in Duluth, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Glenn Jackson Williams | CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Primerica, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $9.0B market cap on $3.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 44% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 36-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 43\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here's Why Primerica (PRI) is a Strong Momentum Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036586/here-s-why-primerica-pri-is-a-strong-momentum-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3036586","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795787403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PRI Raises the Buyback Bar to $500M: A Show of Capital Confidence?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/pri-raises-buyback-bar-500m-120300501.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795608180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (PRI) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_PRI_That_Institutions_Follow_